    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-Organisation---Svc-Excellence---Exec--Customer-Svc---2-year-contract-_JR-10000051798": {
      "title": "Office of Organisation & Svc Excellence – Exec (Customer Svc) (2-year contract)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Office of Organisation & Service Excellence – Executive (Customer Service) (2-year contract) [What you will be working on] As a Customer Service Executive, your key responsibilities include:  • Delivering personalised service to address customer enquiries through email, phone calls, live chats, and in-person interactions at the counter.  • Providing friendly, professional, and efficient service to deliver exceptional customer experiences.  • Identifying and addressing customers’ needs with the goal of achieving high customer satisfaction.  • Using digital service platforms such as case management systems, live chat tools, and customer feedback dashboards to respond to enquiries and track service performance.  • Supporting continuous service improvements by leveraging digital tools and customer insights.  • Leveraging AI and automation tools to deliver easy-to-use services, streamline processes, and enhance overall operational efficiency.  • Handling documentation and administrative tasks, including managing mail, deliveries, and printing of documents. [What we are looking for] To excel in this role, you should possess:  • Proven experience in customer service, preferably in a high-volume or multi-channel environment.  • Strong communication and interpersonal skills.  • Proficiency in administrative work and documentation.  • Ability to multitask and handle various responsibilities efficiently.  • Familiarity with digital customer service platforms (e.g., CRM systems, live chat tools, online forms) and a keen interest in using technology to enhance service delivery.  • Experience or interest in AI, automation, or data-driven tools (e.g., chatbots, Power Automate, Power BI) to improve workflow and service quality is a plus.  • A proactive mindset with a willingness to learn and adapt to evolving responsibilities.  • Excellent organizational and time management skills.  • Ability to work both independently and collaboratively with internal teams and external stakeholders This role is ideal for individuals who thrive in a dynamic, customer-focused environment and are keen to be part of a team that values both human touch and digital innovation in delivering excellent service."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-Student-Support---Senior-Executive-Assistant-Manager-Deputy-Manager_JR-10000050641": {
      "title": "Office of Student Support - Senior Executive/Assistant Manager/Deputy Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Support the design and delivery of RP Talent Development Programme targeted for high performing students, with a focus on student engagement and advisory support. The role involves coordinating stakeholders, creating meaningful developmental opportunities, and guiding students to strengthen scholarship, university and post graduation pathways while building a strong programme community. [What you will be working on] Student Engagement, Advising & Progress Tracking Conduct regular 1-to-1 student check-ins; support students’ goal-setting and action planning. Monitor student progress using established monitoring tools; flag early alerts and coordinate follow-up with schools/stakeholders. Provide advisory support on scholarships, university pathways, internships, careers and further studies, in collaboration with relevant stakeholders and partners. Stakeholder & Partner Engagement Partner schools, parents/guardians (where appropriate) and alumni/industry to strengthen student support, mentoring and exposure. Student Development Opportunities (Local & Overseas) Oversee  local/overseas development opportunities (selection, briefings, logistics, risk management and evaluation); chaperone when required. Student Community Building Plan and lead community-building activities; gather feedback and improve participation and student experience. Guide supporting staff/facilitators/student leaders to ensure consistent engagement and smooth delivery. Management and coordination of communication channels for student engagement (where required). Programme Planning, Delivery & Administration Contribute to the planning, conceptualisation and execution of Talent Development Programme offerings aligned to student developmental needs Support the development of programme content, student resources and communication materials to strengthen student engagement and development and programme delivery. Support budget, procurement and vendor management in accordance with RP policies [What we are looking for] At least 3 years of relevant work experience working with youth in the tertiary education sector A passion for working with people, student centric, empathetic, and able to engage youths effectively Proactive, resourceful, with good time management, stakeholder engagement and collaborative skills Strong written and interpersonal communication skills for working with students, staff and external partners Proficient in Microsoft Tools (Excel, PowerPoint and SharePoint)"
