    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-Student-and-Graduate-Affairs---Assistant-Manager-Senior-Executive_JR-10000050471": {
      "title": "Office of Student and Graduate Affairs - Assistant Manager/Senior Executive",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The successful candidate is required to build and strengthen strategic partnerships with internal and external stakeholders to drive outreach, stakeholder engagement, and RP’s brand through the arts, sports, service-learning, and leadership pillars. This includes identifying new opportunities, managing key partner relationships, and aligning initiatives. This role also requires the candidate to guide staff in delivering impactful Service-Learning experiences that empower students to create meaningful local and global impact. [What you will be working on] •    Manage strategic partnerships with local and international stakeholders (e.g. schools, community groups, agencies)  •    Identify and manage a portfolio of high-impact partners; uncover new partnership opportunities  •    Drive stakeholder alignment and cross-functional coordination for partnership initiatives  •    Plan and execute engagement activities; track outcomes and optimise strategies using data and digital tools  •    Lead and guide staff in delivering Service-Learning projects (primarily local and overseas) and mentor student leaders in the Service-Learning Club to drive growth and impact •    Perform other duties as assigned [What we are looking for] •    At least 3 years of relevant experience in partnership and outreach roles, preferably within the education sector •    Passion for working with people, student-centric, empathetic, and able to engage various stakeholder groups effectively •    Proactive, resourceful, and able to execute and improve operations independently •    Good communication skills for working with community partners, students and staff •    Strong organisational and administrative skills to manage programmes, operations, and resources effectively •    Proficient with marketing and content creation (e.g. social media, visual and video platforms), using visual design and video tools (e.g. Adobe Illustrator, Adobe Premiere Pro, Canva, CapCut, or equivalent platforms) •    Knowledge of MS Office, IT systems, and statistical analysis, automation, productivity, and dashboards (eg: Power Automate, Power BI, etc) will be an added advantage"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-the-Registrar---Assistant-Manager--Admissions-Systems-_JR-10000050432": {
      "title": "Office of the Registrar - Assistant Manager (Admissions Systems)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Office of the Registrar - Assistant Manager (Admissions Systems) [What you will be working on] We are looking for a meticulous and motivated individual to manage and oversee the end-to-end enhancement, testing and rollout of admissions systems supporting Polytechnics and ITE. The role serves as the key liaison between MOE, participating Institutes of Higher Learning (IHLs) and the appointed system vendor to ensure that system enhancements are delivered according to agreed requirements, timelines and quality standards, and are aligned with admissions policies and processes. This position will be on a 2-year contract. Job Description •    Manage and oversee the end-to-end lifecycle of the system enhancement projects, from requirements gathering through development, testing, rollout and post go live support.  •    Keep track of project plans, timelines, issue logs and risk registers to track progress and ensure timely delivery.  •    Monitor vendor deliverables against agreed scope, specifications, milestones and service levels.  •    Escalate project risks, issues and dependencies appropriately, and recommend mitigation actions. •    Work closely with MOE and IHLs to gather, analyse and document business and functional requirements.  •    Translate admissions policies and operational workflows and considerations into clear system requirements. •    Manage User Acceptance Testing (UAT) and coordinate defect logging, triage and resolution with the vendor. •    Support production setup, cutover planning and system rollout activities. •    Monitor system performance post‑deployment and follow through on the rectification of bugs, issues or gaps identified after go‑live. [What we are looking for] •    Relevant qualification with at least 3 years of relevant work in IHL admissions, IT system projects, system enhancements or project coordination. •    Familiarity with admissions processes, Full Subject-Based Banding, student systems or the education sector would be advantageous •    Strong coordination, documentation and stakeholder management skills. •    Able to work effectively with multiple agencies and vendors, with good follow‑through and attention to detail. •    High level of accuracy in data handling and reporting"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-the-Registrar---Deputy-Manager--Student-Records-and-Graduation-_JR-10000053782": {
      "title": "Office of the Registrar - Deputy Manager (Student Records and Graduation)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are looking for a meticulous and motivated individual to manage student records (which include student’s status and particulars, and academic records such as diploma certificates and academic transcripts), and processes and systems relating to student data including deferment, withdrawal and dismissal. Additionally, this role will also be one of the key team members in planning, organising and executing the RP’s graduation ceremony. [What you will be working on] •            Manage processes relating to changes to non-academic and academic student records by ensuring that the processes are user-centric, adhere to guidelines and policies, and optimised via process improvements and use of suitable digitalisation tools. •            Ensure relevant processes are properly documented and kept up-to-date. •            Plan, organise and execute tasks (including procurement, event management and relevant processes, such as registration of graduands, seats and tickets management, on-stage proceedings and display of graduands’ name on screen) for RP’s graduation ceremony. •            Ensure that relevant systems are working according to business requirements, and provide business requirements for new systems or system enhancements and perform User Acceptance Tests (UATs) when required.  •            Prepare data accurately for internal and external reporting in timely manner. [What we are looking for] •    Self-motivated, highly resourceful, and committed individual, capable of working both independently and as part of a team. •    Relevant experience in similar process-focused roles and system-related work, preferably in the education sector.  •    High level of accuracy in data handling and reporting  •    Strong critical thinking, analytical, planning, and organisational skills. •    Proficient in Microsoft Office, Microsoft 365 and digital/automation tools (e.g. SharePoint, Power Automate, RPA)"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-the-Registrar---Manager--Admissions-_JR-10000049140": {
      "title": "Office of the Registrar - Manager (Admissions)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are looking for a meticulous and motivated individual to lead a team of officers in managing full-time diploma admissions, data requests and analysis. The candidate should have good understanding of the tertiary education landscape and be able to recommend strategies for intake planning. Those with vast prior experience and a good track record in managing tertiary admissions or similar operational roles may be considered for a more senior position with a larger job size. [What you will be working on] •    Plan and administer admission exercises, including end-to-end admissions process from application review to offer and enrolment •    Process applications in alignment with institutional policies and admission criteria.  •    Review existing processes and propose enhancements to manage the admission exercises in a timely and accurate manner •    Monitor, analyse and report trends in admissions and course demand •    Manage course streaming and course transfer processes •    Maintain a strong understanding of the admissions policies and procedures, and work with internal stakeholders and external agencies on implementation of admission processes •    Manage systems enhancement and development, including requirement gathering, user acceptance test and data verification •    Review, plan and deliver customer-centric services and procedures •    Manage admissions related enquiries and appeals [What we are looking for] •    Relevant qualification with at least 5 years of relevant work experience with at least 3 years of experience in leading a team •    Prior work experience from another educational institution would be advantageous •    High level of accuracy in data handling and reporting •    Able to multi-task and handle competing priorities within tight timeline •    Strong analytical skills with the ability to work independently as well as in a team •    Excellent communication skills (both spoken and written) and interpersonal skills •    IT savvy and proficient in using Microsoft Office applications •    Knowledge in the use of tools for accurate and efficient analysis of large quantity of data such as Excel VBA, Python or R programming would be advantageous"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Applied-Science---Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Biomedical-Science-_JR-10000054819": {
      "title": "School of Applied Science - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Biomedical Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Applied Science - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Biomedical Science) [What you will be working on] Lecturer will undertake curriculum development and delivery of diploma-related modules as well as be involved in applied science-based research projects. Candidates should possess relevant work or research experience in the Life Science/Biomedical Science Industry.  Job Responsibilities: • Teach relevant subjects in pre-employment and continuing education training programmes • Design and develop course materials for pre-employment and continuing education training programmes • Lead or participate in consultancy and research projects • Supervise students for projects • Mentor and assist in tracking students’ academic and non-academic performance • Partake in administrative duties related to the diploma course or within the school • Deliver planned curriculum for continuing education training programmes on scheduled weekday evenings or weekends and participate in assessment activities [What we are looking for] • Relevant qualification in the field of Life Science/Biomedical Science-related disciplines. • Candidates should possess at least five years of relevant work experience in areas related to Molecular and Cellular Biology, Genetics, Biomedical Informatics, Bioinformatics, Health Informatics and/or Omics.  • Relevant experience with Generative AI, Data Analytics and Sustainability will be advantageous. • Candidates should have strong industry links and exposure, with experience in related sectors. • Candidates should be interested in strengthening the institute's professional network in the Biomedical Science sector • Strong communication and interpersonal skills with ability to build strong working relationships with people at all levels. • Proficient in IT, planning and organising skills."
    },
