      "title": "School of Applied Science - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Biopharma Science & Tech)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Lecturer will undertake curriculum development and delivery of diploma-related modules as well as be involved in applied science-based research projects. Candidates should possess relevant work or research experience in the Biopharmaceutical Manufacturing Industry. [What you will be working on] • Teach relevant subjects in pre-employment and continuing education training programmes • Lead or participate in consultancy and research projects • Design and develop course materials for pre-employment and continuing education training programmes • Supervise students for projects • Mentor and assist in tracking students’ academic and non-academic performance • Partake in administrative duties related to the diploma course or within the school • Deliver planned curriculum to adult learners on scheduled weekday evenings or on weekends and participate in assessment activities [What we are looking for] • Relevant qualification in the field of Life Science/Pharmaceutical Science-related disciplines. • Candidates should possess at least five years of relevant work experience in areas related to Bioprocessing, Quality Control and Assurance, Manufacturing Science and Technology and/or Healthcare Supply Chain. • Candidates should have strong industry links and exposure, with experience in related sectors • Candidates should be interested in strengthening the institute's professional network in the Pharmaceutical Manufacturing sector • Relevant experience with Generative AI, Data Analytics and Sustainability will be advantageous. • Proficient in IT, planning, and organisation skills • Strong communication and interpersonal skills"
