    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Business---Assoc-Lecturer--Digital-Business-and-Banking-and-Finance-_JR-10000054349": {
      "title": "School of Business - Assoc Lecturer (Digital Business and Banking and Finance)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] As an Adjunct Lecturer, you will bring current industry knowledge into the classroom and help young and adult learners develop practical, workplace-relevant skills. Depending on the modules assigned, you will deliver lessons, facilitate applied learning and assess students in one of the specialisations below. [What you will be working on] Key Responsibilities •    Deliver scheduled lessons and facilitate learning for Pre-Employment Training (PET) and/or Continuing Education and Training (CET) students. •    Prepare for classes using the approved curriculum and learning resources, and adapt delivery to support learners with different needs. •    Facilitate hands-on activities, case discussions and problem-based learning using relevant industry examples and tools. •    Assess students' work, provide timely feedback and complete grading and related academic administration within stipulated timelines. •    Provide consultation and learning support to students for the assigned module. •    Contribute industry insights to the review of lesson materials, assessments or applied projects where required. •    Comply with RP's academic, assessment and administrative requirements. Areas of Specialisation Candidates should be able to teach in at least one of the following areas: 1. Digital Solutions and Business Technology •    Digital Business, AI, Automation, Data Visualisation, Business Technologies and Project Deployment. •    Application of AI tools, workflow automation, CRM, analytics, e-commerce and low-code/no-code platforms to business problems. •    Business needs analysis, solution design, prototyping, testing and basic technical troubleshooting. 2. Banking and Finance •    Financial Technology, Analytics, Financial Markets, Corporate Finance, Investment Analysis, Trade Finance, Compliance, Risk Management and Sustainable Finance. •    Application of real-world case studies, simulations and tools such as Excel, data analytics and AI applications. [What we are looking for] General Requirements •    Relevant academic qualifications in Business, Banking, Finance, Economics, Data Analytics, Business Technology or a related field. •    At least three years of relevant industry experience. Prior teaching, training or facilitation experience is advantageous. •    Current industry knowledge and the ability to translate professional experience into practical learning. •    A nurturing mindset and the ability to establish a strong rapport with learners. •    Strong communication and facilitation skills, with the ability to explain concepts clearly. •    Reliable, organised and able to meet teaching, assessment and administrative timelines. •    Comfortable using relevant digital and educational technologies for lesson delivery. 1. Digital Solutions and Business Technology •    Relevant experience in digital transformation, technology implementation, business analysis, product or project management, automation, CRM, e-commerce, marketing technology or data analytics. •    Hands-on experience in deploying digital, automation or AI-enabled solutions, including workflows, prototypes or proof-of-concept solutions. •    Able to analyse business problems, explain solution logic and troubleshoot basic issues involving workflows, configurations, data, integrations and outputs. •    Shortlisted candidates may be asked to showcase a prior AI workflow or solution and present a short demonstration and teaching deck for a proposed one-hour lesson, including their lesson-design thought process. 2. Banking and Finance •    Strong expertise in one or more areas: banking operations; risk, compliance and AML/KYC; financial markets, treasury or investment products; fintech, digital banking or data analytics; sustainable finance or ESG. •    Good understanding of trends shaping the financial sector, including digitalisation, AI, regulation and sustainability. •    Relevant professional certifications such as CFA, FRM, IBF or sustainability-related credentials are advantageous."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Business---Associate-Lecturer--Accounting-or-Taxation-or-Audit-_JR-10000042268": {
      "title": "School of Business – Associate Lecturer (Accounting)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] As an Associate Lecturer with the School of Business, you will facilitate authentic and engaging learning experiences that prepare students for the workplace through learner-centred and industry-relevant education. [What you will be working on] •    Facilitate engaging and experiential learning using Republic Polytechnic's Problem-Based Learning (PBL) pedagogy and other learner-centred approaches. •    Deliver lessons and facilitate learning in accordance with approved curricula, assessment requirements and academic standards. •    Assess students' learning through assignments, projects, presentations and other assessment methods, and provide timely, constructive feedback. •    Mentor and guide students in their academic and professional development, fostering a positive and inclusive learning environment. •    Work collaboratively with Module Chairs and academic teams to ensure effective curriculum delivery and continuous enhancement of the student learning experience. •    Teach and contribute to one or more of the following areas:    o Financial and Management Accounting    o Audit & Assurance    o Taxation    o Sustainable Finance ESG & Sustainability Reporting     o AI & Digital Technologies in Accounting    o Risk, Regulatory Compliance and Corporate Governance    o Business Law and Company Law [What we are looking for] •   Relevant qualifications in accounting, or a related discipline. A postgraduate qualification will be an advantage. •    Professional qualifications such as ACCA, CA Singapore, ICAEW, CPA Australia or equivalent are preferred. •    At least 5 years of relevant industry experience in accounting, audit, taxation, sustainability reporting, risk management, or regulatory compliance. •    Ability to teach both Pre-Employment Training (PET) students and Continuing Education and Training (CET) adult learners. •    Strong communication, facilitation and interpersonal skills. •    Experience in teaching, training or coaching will be an advantage."
    },
