    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Business---CET-Associate-Lecturer--Business-_JR-10000054827": {
      "title": "School of Business - CET Associate Lecturer (Business)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] School of Business - CET Associate Lecturer (Business) [What you will be working on] Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: • Teach relevant subjects in Continuing Education Training (CET) programmes •    Design and develop course materials for Continuing Education Training (CET) programmes in Business, Management, Marketing, Human Resources, Accounting, Finance, Sustainability, Digital Business, Artificial Intelligence, Entrepreneurship, or other related disciplines. •    Deliver planned curriculum to adult learners on scheduled weekday evenings or on weekends and participate in assessment activities •    Take up the role of Programme Coordinator for CET module when required [What we are looking for] •    Relevant qualifications in Business, Management, Marketing, Human Resources, Accounting, Finance, Sustainability, Digital Business, Artificial Intelligence, Entrepreneurship, or other related disciplines.  •    At least five years of relevant industry experience in one or more business domains, such as marketing, digital transformation, human resources, finance, accounting, business operations, sustainability, entrepreneurship, or organisational development.  •    Training and Adult Education (TAE) Workforce Skills Qualification (WSQ) certifications such as Advanced Certificate in Learning and Performance (ACLP), Advanced Certificate in Training and Assessment (ACTA), or Diploma in Adult and Continuing Education (DACE) will be advantageous.  •    Passion for adult learning and the ability to facilitate learning for working professionals from diverse backgrounds.  •    Strong communication, presentation and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage learners effectively and build strong working relationships with industry partners and stakeholders.  •    Sound planning, organisational and classroom facilitation skills, with a practical and learner-centric approach.  •    Proficient in the use of digital learning technologies, productivity tools and online collaboration platforms.  •    Prior experience in curriculum development, training delivery, coaching, mentoring, consultancy, or industry projects will be an added advantage."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Singapore/School-of-Business---Lecturer--Business-_JR-10000042267": {
      "title": "School of Business - Lecturer (Business)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The job of a lecturer is immensely meaningful and significant. You will impart knowledge and skills, prepare young and adult learners for the working world, and nurture their development. The role also offers opportunities to develop contemporary curricula, conduct impactful lessons, participate in consultancy and applied research, and collaborate with industry partners. [What you will be working on] Core Responsibilities •    Deliver lessons, develop teaching and assessment materials, and facilitate learning for Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) students. •    Enhance existing and/or develop new curricula and learning materials to strengthen students’ application and employability. •    Contribute to PET and CET modules and programmes, using appropriate GenAI and EdTech tools where applicable. •    Participate in the development of teaching and learning capabilities within RP and the School’s academic team. •    Support the School’s strategic initiatives through academic advancement, student development and industry projects. •    Undertake academic administration, including setting assessments, grading submissions and coordinating academic reports. •    Provide pastoral support and guide students through internships, final-year projects, competitions, career development and overseas learning activities. Areas of Specialisation Candidates are expected to contribute in at least one of the following specialisations: 1. Digital Solutions and Business Technology •    Design and deliver modules in Digital Business, AI, Automation, Data Visualisation, Business Technologies and Project Deployment. •    Guide students in analysing business needs and designing practical technology-enabled solutions. •    Conduct hands-on learning using AI tools, workflow automation, CRM, analytics, e-commerce and low-code/no-code platforms. •    Support digital and AI consultancy projects from requirements gathering and solution design to testing and deployment. •    Teach students to explore new and emerging technologies, troubleshoot basic technical issues and improve their solutions. 2. Banking and Finance •    Design and deliver modules in Financial Technology, Analytics and areas such as Financial Markets, Corporate Finance, Investment Analysis, Trade Finance, Compliance, Risk Management and Sustainable Finance. •    Integrate real-world case studies, simulations and industry-relevant tools such as Excel, data analytics and AI applications into learning. •    Collaborate with banks, fintech firms, regulators and professional bodies to co-develop curricula, projects and experiential learning opportunities. •    Participate in consultancy, applied research and capability-building initiatives related to banking, finance and sustainability. [What we are looking for] General Requirements •    Relevant academic qualifications in Business, Banking, Finance, Economics, Data Analytics, Marketing, Business Technology or a related field. •    A nurturing mindset and the ability to establish a strong rapport with learners. •    Strong industry connections that can bring real-world context and opportunities into the learning experience. •    Ability to integrate relevant technology and current industry developments into teaching and learning. •    A collaborative, self-driven and resourceful team player who can manage multiple projects independently. •    Strong communication, facilitation, project and stakeholder management skills. 1. Digital Solutions and Business Technology •    At least three years of relevant experience in digital transformation, technology implementation, business analysis, product or project management, automation, CRM, e-commerce, marketing technology or data analytics. Teaching or training experience is an advantage. •    Experience in managing or deploying digital, automation, technology or AI-enabled projects. •    Ability to analyse business problems, identify root causes and translate needs into practical solution requirements. •    Comfortable exploring new technologies and troubleshooting workflows, configurations, data, integrations and outputs. •    Experience in developing and testing prototypes, proof-of-concept solutions, digital workflows or process improvements. •    Able to explain technical concepts clearly to non-technical learners and stakeholders. 2. Banking and Finance •    At least three years of relevant experience in banking, financial services, fintech or a related sector. Teaching or training experience is an advantage. •    Strong expertise in one or more areas: banking operations; risk, compliance and AML/KYC; financial markets, treasury or investment products; fintech, digital banking or data analytics; sustainable finance or ESG. •    Good understanding of trends shaping the financial sector, including digitalisation, AI, regulation and sustainability. •    Experience with financial institutions, fintech firms, regulators or professional bodies is advantageous. •    Relevant certifications such as CFA, FRM, IBF or sustainability-related credentials are a bonus."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Business---Lecturer--Mass-Communication-_JR-10000053841": {
      "title": "School of Business - Lecturer (Mass Communication)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Business - Lecturer (Mass Communication) [What you will be working on] Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: •    Develop, facilitate and enhance curriculum for diploma and adult learners in one or more areas, including:         -     Digital media and content strategy         -     Video production, storytelling and multimedia content creation         -     Public relations and corporate communications         -     Generative AI for content creation and communication •    Design authentic learning experiences using real-world briefs, industry practices, emerging technologies and applied projects. •    Develop assessments, rubrics and feedback approaches that support professional communication practice. •    Supervise student projects, internships and industry collaborations. •    Source and manage industry partnerships, projects and experiential learning opportunities. •    Mentor students in communication practice, portfolio development, employability, ethics and responsible use of technology like Gen AI. [What we are looking for] •    Relevant qualifications in Communications, Media, Journalism, Public Relations, Digital Marketing, or related fields. •    At least 5 years of relevant industry experience. •    Strong industry networks and ability to establish partnerships that create authentic learning opportunities for students. •    Familiarity with Generative AI tools and their responsible use in communication, content creation, editing, fact-checking and audience engagement. •    Excellent written, spoken and interpersonal communication skills, with a good command of English. •    A collaborative, agile and student-centred mindset, with a passion for developing future-ready communication professionals."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Assistant-Manager-Deputy-Manager_JR-10000052471": {
      "title": "School of Engineering - Senior Executive/Assistant Manager",
