      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Engineering - Lecturer (Electrical Engineering, Semiconductor Technology & Manufacturing) [What you will be working on] •    Deliver and develop lessons in electrical engineering, electronics, microelectronics and semiconductor technology.  •    Teach topics such as circuit analysis, analogue and digital electronics, semiconductor devices, IC fundamentals, instrumentation and engineering applications.  •    Deliver semiconductor modules covering wafer fabrication, process integration, semiconductor manufacturing, testing, packaging, reliability and yield engineering.  •    Develop curriculum, laboratories and projects involving AI-enabled semiconductor manufacturing, smart factories, semiconductor data analytics, intelligent process control, computer vision and Industry 4.0 technologies.  •    Develop and conduct CET programmes, including Specialist Diploma and Part-time Diploma courses.  •    Supervise student projects, internships and applied learning activities.  •    Collaborate with industry and university partners on curriculum development, applied projects and industry engagement.  •    Support outreach activities, student development and administrative duties. [What we are looking for] •    Strong fundamentals in electronics, electrical engineering, semiconductor devices and microelectronics.  •    Knowledge or exposure in one or more areas:  •    Semiconductor manufacturing and wafer fabrication •    Equipment, process or product engineering •    Testing, reliability or yield engineering •    Advanced packaging or semiconductor automation •    Interest or experience in AI for semiconductor applications, including:      - Yield prediction     - Defect detection and classification     - Computer vision for wafer inspection     - Predictive maintenance     - Manufacturing analytics     - Digital twins     - Smart manufacturing and Industry 4.0     - AI-enabled process optimisation •    Exposure to emerging technologies such as advanced packaging, chiplets, silicon photonics, AI accelerators, high-bandwidth memory (HBM) or SiC/GaN devices will be advantageous. •    Ability to utilise AI tools for engineering, teaching and applied projects.  •    Passion for teaching, mentoring and engaging youths.  •    Strong communication and interpersonal skills."
