      "title": "School of Engineering - Lecturer (Mobility & Robotic Systems)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Engineering - Lecturer (Mobility & Robotic Systems) [What you will be working on] •    Curriculum development, course delivery and student project supervision in the areas of large mobility and smart robotic engineering systems. This includes, but is not limited to, automation, manufacturing, advanced robotic systems such as Industry 4.0/5.0 and Intelligent Transport Systems, including Autonomous Vehicles (AVs) and Electric Vehicles (EVs).  •    Develop and conduct Continuing Education and Training (CET) lessons. •    Spearhead and identify new opportunities, initiatives and collaborations with industry. •    Undertake project development or consultancy work with industry. •    Perform other administrative work related to the programme. •    Undertake student development activities. •    Mentor and motivate students in their learning journey. [What we are looking for] •    Qualification in electrical / electronic / mechanical / mechatronic engineering or a related discipline, preferably with at least 1 year of experience in design, deployment, and commissioning of robotics, automation systems, or Intelligent Transport Systems. •    Possess excellent initiative, strong multitasking skills, and a strong sense of responsibility for completing assigned duties on time. •    Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively as an excellent team player. •    Comfortable with programming and electronics, such as Arduino, Raspberry Pi, Python, or similar platforms, hands-on experiences in Robotics, Robot Operating System (ROS), Robot Programming, Industry 4.0/5.0, Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT), Collaborative/Mobile Robots or Intelligent Transport Systems will be an advantage."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Lecturer--Sustainable-Built-Environment-_JR-10000053811": {
      "title": "School of Engineering - Lecturer (Sustainable Built Environment)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Engineering - Lecturer (Sustainable Built Environment) [What you will be working on] •    Design and deliver lessons to full-time diploma students in areas such as Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning (HVAC), Air Conditioning and Mechanical Ventilation (ACMV), Building Services Engineering, energy management, Green Buildings, sustainability and related Built Environment disciplines. •    Integrate industry-relevant technologies and practices such as smart building systems, building analytics, digitalisation and Artificial Intelligence (AI) applications into teaching and learning. •    Develop and conduct Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes for adult learners and industry professionals. •    Design assessments and undertake curriculum development, course delivery and student learning responsibilities. •    Supervise student internships, final-year projects and industry-based learning activities. •    Mentor and guide students in their academic, professional and personal development. •    Initiate, lead and manage Technology, Innovation and Enterprise (TIE) projects, including industry consultancy, commissioned projects, applied research and innovation initiatives. •    Identify opportunities for industry-funded projects, grants and collaborations with companies, government agencies and professional bodies. •    Build and maintain strong partnerships with stakeholders in the Built Environment sector to support education, innovation and industry engagement. •    Participate in programme administration, outreach activities and other school-wide initiatives. [What we are looking for] •    Qualification in Mechanical Engineering, Building Services Engineering, Sustainable Built Environment, Facilities Management, Energy Engineering, Architecture, Engineering or a related discipline. •    Preferably with at least 3 years of relevant industry experience in Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning (HVAC), Air Conditioning and Mechanical Ventilation (ACMV), Green Mark consultancy, Building Services Engineering, energy efficiency, sustainability, Facilities Management, or related Built Environment sectors. •    Strong technical knowledge in ACMV/HVAC systems, energy-efficient building services, building energy performance, Green Mark requirements and sustainable building technologies. •    Familiarity with smart building systems, building analytics, digitalisation, Artificial Intelligence (AI), Internet of Things (IoT), Building Information Modelling (BIM) or related technologies would be advantageous. •    Experience in managing or participating in industry projects, consultancy assignments, commissioned projects, grant-funded projects or innovation initiatives would be advantageous. •    Passionate about education and committed to nurturing both youth and adult learners. •    Strong communication, presentation and stakeholder management skills. •    Possess sound planning, organisational and project management skills, with a strong sense of responsibility and the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. •    Self-motivated and able to work independently as well as collaboratively in multidisciplinary teams."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Project-Staff--Robotics-and-Unmanned-Systems-_JR-10000053820": {
      "title": "School of Engineering - Project Staff (Robotics and Unmanned Systems)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are seeking a versatile and forward-thinking Development Engineer/Specialist to join our team in advancing the boundaries of Physical and Embodied AI. In this role, you will bridge the gap between intelligent software and the physical world, transforming AI models into tangible, autonomous capabilities. You will design, prototype, and deploy AI-enabled physical systems—such as robotics, unmanned platforms, and smart automation solutions—utilizing ROS2.0. You will also act as a bridge between technology, industry partners, and academia, fostering ecosystem growth through knowledge sharing, mentoring student projects, and leading live innovation showcases. If you are passionate about applied research, hands-on hardware-software integration, and inspiring others, we want to hear from you. [What you will be working on] 1. Physical & Embodied AI Development •    System Design & Prototyping: Design, develop, and prototype intelligent physical systems, robotics, and advanced automation platforms leveraging ROS2.0. •    Hardware-Software Integration: Integration of advanced AI models, computer vision, and operational systems with sensors, actuators, edge devices, and embedded systems. •    Applied Research & Piloting: Drive feasibility studies and pilot programs involving AI-enabled automation, unmanned systems (UAVs/AGVs), and smart monitoring solutions. •    End-to-End Project Support: Manage the full lifecycle of applied research and proof-of-concept initiatives, including data preparation, rigorous experimentation, performance evaluation, comprehensive documentation, and post-deployment technical support. •    Prototype Commercialization: Assist in translating high-potential AI prototypes into scalable, deployable, or licensable industry solutions. 2. Knowledge Sharing & Ecosystem Enablement •    Educational Mentorship: Support curriculum development and actively mentor student capstone and research projects in robotics and applied AI domains. •    Stakeholder Collaboration: Partner closely with internal researchers and external industry stakeholders on collaborative innovation initiatives. •    Technology Advocacy: Lead and support engaging AI and robotics demonstrations for lab visits, innovation showcases, and executive partner engagements. •    Use Case Curation: Synthesize and curate compelling physical AI use cases to engage, educate, and inspire both academic and industrial audiences. [What we are looking for] •    Qualification in Robotics Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical/Electronic Engineering, Mechatronics, or a closely related quantitative field. •    Robotics Architecture: Proven hands-on experience developing with ROS2 (Robot Operating System). Familiarity with robotic arms and humanoid robots, robot kinematics, dynamics, and simulation tools (e.g., Gazebo, Isaac Sim) is highly valued. •    AI & Computer Vision Integration: Practical experience deploying Machine Learning/Deep Learning models (e.g., PyTorch, TensorFlow) and computer vision frameworks (e.g., OpenCV) onto physical platforms. •    Embedded Software Engineering: Proficiency in C++ and Python, with strong software development best practices (Git, clean architecture, code reviews). •    Hardware & Edge Systems: Experience working with microcontrollers and single-board computers (e.g., NVIDIA Jetson, Raspberry Pi). Solid understanding of hardware communication protocols (I2C, SPI, UART, CAN bus) and sensor fusion (LiDAR, IMUs, cameras). Soft Skills & Core Attributes •    Collaborative Mindset: Exceptional interpersonal skills with a proven ability to collaborate effectively across diverse teams of engineers, researchers, students, and corporate partners. •    Communication & Presentation: Confident and articulate presenter capable of breaking down complex technical concepts into accessible demonstrations for non-technical audiences. •    Passion in Educational Mentorship: Guiding student learning journeys and contributing to educational frameworks. •    Adaptability: A thriving curiosity for ambiguous, fast-paced R&D environments where troubleshooting physical hardware requires creative problem-solving."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Research-Staff--Aquaculture-Water-Treatment-_JR-10000054858-1": {
      "title": "School of Engineering - Research Staff (Aquaculture Water Treatment)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Republic Polytechnic's School of Engineering (SEG), in collaboration with the School of Science (SAS), invites applications for a full-time Research Staff on a 12-month contract to support the DGF-funded project, \"Smart Water Treatment in Recirculating Aquaculture Systems (RAS) for Land-based Fish Farms.\" This applied R&D project focuses on developing an innovative smart water treatment system to improve water quality, reduce ammonia, pathogens, turbidity, biofilm, and algae, and enhance the sustainability of land-based aquaculture. The project integrates two proprietary technologies: •    DuoBioSonic – Dual-frequency ultrasonic cavitation for controlling pathogens, algae, biofilm, and turbidity.  •    AquAPEX – Multicellular graphite electrolysis for ammonia and nitrogen removal.  The successful candidate will contribute to prototype development, laboratory research, system integration, water quality analysis, field validation at commercial fish farms, and technology commercialisation. [What you will be working on] Key Responsibilities: •    Conduct applied research on smart water treatment technologies for recirculating aquaculture systems (RAS).  •    Perform laboratory experiments, aquaculture field trials, water quality monitoring, microbiological testing, and data analysis.  •    Develop, integrate, and evaluate prototype systems, sensors, and instrumentation.  •    Collaborate with industry partners to support technology validation and deployment.  •    Supervise final-year project students and interns involved in the project.  •    Support intellectual property (IP) development, technology transfer, and commercialisation activities.  •    Prepare technical reports, journal publications, presentations, and research grant proposals.  •    Manage laboratory equipment & consumables, procurement, safety compliance, and research products. [What we are looking for] •    Qualification in Environmental Engineering/Science, Water Engineering, Aquaculture Science, Marine/Ocean Engineering/Science, Chemical Engineering, Biotechnology, Applied Chemistry, Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics, Biomedical Science, Food Science, Systems Engineering, or a related field. •    Interest in water treatment, aquaculture, water quality monitoring, microbiology, and applied research. •    Knowledge of sensors, instrumentation, experimental design, data acquisition, and data analysis is an advantage. •    Experience in laboratory testing, microbiological analysis, aquaculture, or water quality assessment is preferred. •    Self-motivated, hands-on, and able to work independently and in multidisciplinary teams of researchers, engineers, scientists and students. •    Good report/technical writing skills. •    Entry-level candidates are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Research-Staff--Cold-Storage---Cryogenic-Systems-_JR-10000054861": {
      "title": "School of Engineering - Research Staff (Cold Storage & Cryogenic Systems)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Are you ready to build next-generation, sustainable cold chain logistics for life-saving biopharmaceuticals? Republic Polytechnic's School of Engineering (SEG), in strategic partnership with industry leader SSW Group, is seeking an ambitious full-time Research Staff (12-month contract) to engineer an industrial-scale 1\"m\" ^3 self-sustained passive cold storage platform under a DGF-funded initiative. Current biopharmaceutical distribution relies on massive active energy inputs and heavy daily coolant consumption. This project completely disrupts that model by building a zero-power-in-transit, high-performance thermal container (1\"m\"×1\"m\"×1\"m\" ) capable of locking in sub-zero temperatures (2–8°C) for over 72 continuous hours in harsh tropical environments. Beyond standard transport, this passive design provides critical fail-safe protection against warehouse power outages and opens up new pathways for long-haul air and sea freight to distant international markets without relying on active electrical refrigeration networks. You will lead the hands-on engineering across two breakthrough technological pillars: - Active-Passive \"Flash-Charging\" Cryogenic System: A rapid-charging base station interface utilizing specialized heat exchangers and Liquid Nitrogen (LN_2) bursts to charge high-density Phase Change Material (PCM) cores and Vacuum Insulated Panels (VIP). - Triple-Vector IoT Telemetry Engine: An ultra-low-power, cloud-connected sensor matrix tracking real-time Temperature, Relative Humidity, and Oxygen (O_2) levels to ensure absolute data transparency and regulatory compliance (HSA/FDA standards). The successful candidate will contribute to prototype development, laboratory research, system integration, cold box temperature analysis, field validation at mimic cold storage environment, and technology commercialisation. [What you will be working on] - Perform 3D CAD modelling, understand basic fluid dynamics, and heat exchanger design to eliminate thermal dead zones and maximize LN_2 thermodynamic efficiency across a 1\"m\" ^3 volume. - Design, route, and balance high-pressure LN_2 cryogenic pipelines, vacuum-jacketed tubings, manifolds, and automated valve safety systems. - Build IOT, test, and integrate low-power microcontrollers and sensor arrays (Temp,RH,O_2) with live, cloud-based telemetry dashboards. - Perform laboratory experiments, cold storage environment trials, temperature and humidity monitoring, passive cold storage box testing, and data analysis.  - Develop, integrate, and evaluate prototype systems, sensors, and instrumentation.  - Collaborate with industry partners to support technology validation and deployment.  - Supervise final-year project students and interns involved in the project.  - Support intellectual property (IP) development, technology transfer, and commercialisation activities.  - Prepare technical reports, journal publications, presentations, and research grant proposals.  - Manage laboratory equipment & consumables, procurement, safety compliance, and research products. [What we are looking for] - Qualification in Mechanical Engineering, Thermal/Fluid Engineering, Mechatronics, Electrical & Electronic Engineering, Systems Engineering, Materials Science, or a related discipline. - Have basic foundational understanding of thermodynamics, fluid dynamics, heat transfer, or cold-chain storage technologies. - Proficiency in 3D CAD modelling (Autodesk Fusion 360 or SolidWorks) and Design for Manufacturing (DFM) principles. - Practical skills in embedded electronics, microcontroller programming (Arduino / ESP32), and IoT sensor integration. - Experience or have interest in cryogenic fluids (LN_2), heat exchangers, or fluid pipeline design is a major advantage. - A hands-on, proactive mindset with the drive to build physical prototypes and lead projects independently in a dynamic lab environment. - Strong technical writing and data presentation skills. - Entry-level candidates with strong final-year project experience in thermal fluids, mechatronics, or smart hardware are highly encouraged to apply."
    },
