    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Events---Project-Management-_JR-10000038281-1": {
      "title": "School of Hospitality - Lecturer (Events & Project Management)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Republic Polytechnic is seeking passionate and industry-experienced professionals to join the Diploma in Events & Project Management (DEPM). We are looking for individuals who are committed to developing future-ready graduates equipped with competencies in event management, project leadership, experience design, digital transformation, sustainability, and Artificial Intelligence (AI). As a Lecturer, you will play a pivotal role in shaping the next generation of event and project management professionals equipped with versatile strategic and operational competencies. Your responsibilities extend beyond teaching to encompass nurturing students' potential, curriculum innovation, industry engagement, consultancy projects, and applied learning initiatives. [What you will be working on] Teaching and Learning Facilitate learning for Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education & Training (CET) programmes in areas such as: Curriculum Development •    Design, develop and review curriculum, learning resources and assessments to ensure industry relevance and alignment with emerging workforce needs. •    Integrate industry practices, digital technologies and AI-enabled tools into teaching and learning. •    Develop authentic, industry-based learning experiences that enhance students’ employability and professional competencies. •    Contribute to the development of stackable credentials, professional certifications and lifelong learning programmes. Industry Engagement and Applied Learning •    Establish and maintain strong partnerships with industry stakeholders, professional associations and government agencies. •    Initiate and manage industry projects, consultancy engagements and work-integrated learning opportunities. •    Mentor students participating in competitions, industry showcases and experiential learning activities. •    Facilitate industry visits, guest lectures and networking opportunities. AI and Digital Innovation •    Champion the adoption of AI and emerging technologies within teaching, learning and industry projects. •    Guide students in the responsible and effective use of AI tools for project planning, event operations, marketing, content creation, stakeholder engagement and data analysis. •    Explore and integrate emerging technologies such as Generative AI, Agentic AI, workflow automation, data analytics and digital experience platforms where relevant. Student Development •    Mentor and support students in their academic, professional and personal development. •    Supervise internships, final-year projects and industry-based assignments. •    Foster the development of leadership, communication, collaboration and problem-solving skills. Professional and Institutional Contributions •    Contribute to consultancy, applied research and capability development initiatives. •    Design and deliver professional development programmes and customised training solutions for industry partners. •    Participate in school-wide and institution-wide projects, committees and strategic initiatives. [What we are looking for] •    Relevant tertiary qualification in Events Management, Project Management, Hospitality, Tourism, Business, Marketing, Communications or a related discipline. •    Postgraduate qualifications will be an advantage. Industry Experience •    Minimum 8 years of relevant industry experience in one or more of the following areas: o    MICE and Business Events o    Conferences and Exhibitions o    Event Production and Live Events o    Project Management o    Customer Experience and Experience Design o    Event Technology and Digital Experiences o    Marketing and Communications o    Tourism and Destination Management Professional Competencies •    Strong industry knowledge and practical experience in event and project management. •    Experience leading cross-functional projects and managing multiple stakeholders. •    Excellent communication, presentation and facilitation skills. •    Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to build and maintain industry partnerships. •    Passion for coaching, mentoring and developing youths and adult learners. •    Self-motivated, adaptable and committed to continuous learning. AI and Digital Competencies Candidates should demonstrate an interest in, and practical application of, technology and AI within professional settings. Experience in any of the following areas will be advantageous: •    AI-assisted productivity and collaboration tools •    Workflow automation platforms •    Digital marketing technologies •    Data analytics and visualisation tools •    Customer relationship management (CRM) platforms •    Event technology and engagement solutions •    Digital transformation initiatives"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer_JR-10000042269": {
      "title": "School of Hospitality - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are seeking a dynamic and passionate individual to join RP as a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in the School of Hospitality. In this pivotal role which goes beyond teaching and facilitating learning, you will foster the aspirations of individual students and nurture their lifelong learning needs. Your dedication and expertise will contribute to shaping their educational journey and preparing them for future success. You are expected to conduct academic research by way of detailed observations, analyses findings, interpretation of results for potential applications and publish papers on the completed studies in peer-reviewed, well-respected journals and/or educational conferences. [What you will be working on] •    Foster a nurturing environment for students through comprehensive pastoral care and offer guidance and support in their educational and career journeys. •    Develop and review module curriculum with engaging learning activities that align with the prescribed programme and module outcomes for both pre-employment training (PET) and continuing education and training (CET). •    Deliver lessons effectively through good class management and with efficacious outcomes. •    Supervise students in projects and other curricular activities.  •    Conduct academic/action research projects to continuously develop and deepen competencies in teaching and learning. •    Undertake administrative duties and academic affairs related to a programme.  [What we are looking for] •    Possess excellent interpersonal, communication, management, and writing skills. •    Demonstrate resourcefulness as a team player while exhibiting trustworthiness, independence, and a proactive work ethic. •    Strong conceptual thinking skills with an ability to problem solve and recommend solutions. •    Able to facilitate classroom discussions, adeptly mediate different opinions and evaluate reasoning. •    Able to introduce effective interventions by analysing students' results and performance. •    Preferably with academic research experience, publication, and successful funding/grant applications.  •    Digital literacy (using information ethically and effectively), and the ability to collaborate and communicate using digital tools. •    AI literacy that includes AI fundamentals, data science, AI tools and automation, Natural Language Processing (NLP), AI ethics, and prompt engineering. •    A minimum of five years of teaching experience, preferably teaching subjects in any of the following areas:  >    Hospitality Business Management >    Customer Experience Management >    Customer Journey Mapping and Analytics"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Senior-Lecturer--Capabilities---Industry-Development-_JR-10000054835": {
      "title": "School of Hospitality - Senior Lecturer (Capabilities & Industry Development)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Hospitality - Senior Lecturer (Capabilities & Industry Development) [What you will be working on] The School of Hospitality is seeking an experienced hospitality professional with expertise in hotel management, business development, and tech & innovation. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching and learning, drive hospitality transformation projects, develop strategic partnerships, and lead initiatives that enhance industry capabilities through technology and innovation. Teaching & Learning •    Teach and facilitate learning in hospitality-related modules, including hotel operations, guest experience management, hospitality technology, and service innovation. •    Develop and review curriculum to ensure alignment with evolving industry needs and emerging technologies. •    Mentor and supervise students in projects, internships, and industry-based learning activities. •    Integrate industry practices, digital tools, and experiential learning approaches into teaching and assessment. Hospitality & Digital Innovation Projects •    Lead industry projects and consultancy initiatives focused on hotel operations, guest experience, and hospitality transformation. •    Drive the adoption and application of emerging hospitality technologies, including Artificial Intelligence, data analytics and business intelligence, smart hotel and Internet of Things solutions, Property Management Systems, Customer Relationship Management platforms, and contactless guest experience technologies. •    Identify, develop, and implement innovative solutions that enhance operational efficiency, service quality, and customer experience. •    Manage hospitality innovation and capability-development projects, including project planning, stakeholder engagement, resource coordination, risk management, and delivery of project outcomes. •    Conduct applied research and collaborate with industry partners to address business challenges and support workforce transformation. Business Development & Industry Engagement •    Build and maintain partnerships with hotels, hospitality organisations, technology providers, and government agencies. •    Identify and secure opportunities for consultancy, executive education, applied research, and collaborative industry projects. •    Develop proposals, business cases, and partnership agreements. •    Represent the School at industry forums, conferences, and networking events. [What we are looking for] •    Relevant qualification(s) in Hospitality Management, Hotel Administration, Tourism, Business, Information Systems, Digital Transformation, or a related discipline. A postgraduate qualification is advantageous. •    At least 8 years of relevant industry experience in hotel management, hospitality consulting, hospitality technology, tourism, or a related sector. •    Strong understanding of hotel operations and hospitality technologies. •    Experience in hospitality digital transformation, smart hospitality solutions, AI applications, service innovation, or customer experience enhancement. •    Proven track record in business development, industry engagement, and partnership management. •    Strong project leadership and stakeholder management skills. •    Excellent communication, presentation, facilitation, and relationship-building abilities. Preferred Attributes •    Passion for hospitality innovation and digital transformation. •    Strong industry network within the hospitality and tourism sectors. •    Ability to bridge industry practice with applied education and research. •    Self-motivated, adaptable, and collaborative team player."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Singapore/School-of-Infocomm---Assistant-Director-Capability-and-Industry_JR-10000036994": {
      "title": "School of Infocomm - Assistant Director Capability and Industry",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The Assistant Director (Capability and Industry) is a strategic and hands-on technology leader with deep expertise in artificial intelligence, capability development, and business development. This role is responsible for crafting and executing strategies that advance the School's goals in capability building and industry engagement. We are looking for individuals with a proven track record of translating advanced technologies into impactful business solutions, driving organizational capability, and leading cross-functional teams in dynamic and complex environments. [What you will be working on] •    Spearhead capability development initiatives to strengthen the School’s technology capabilities, focusing on artificial intelligence and emerging technologies.  •    Monitor and anticipate industry trends, evolving skillsets, and solution needs to ensure the School remains at the forefront of IT innovation. •    Align departmental competencies to develop and implement a technology roadmap supporting the School’s long-term strategic goals. •    Oversee the planning and delivery of technology projects and training programmes in the emerging technology domains. •    Lead, coach and develop high-performing teams to drive successful industry projects and impactful training programmes. •    Forge strategic partnerships with industry leaders, academic institutions, government agencies and other key stakeholders to expand the School's reach and influence. •    Represent the School at industry events, conferences, and forums to enhance visibility, build partnerships, and stay abreast of the latest industry developments. •    Drive business growth by identifying new opportunities, developing go-to-market strategies, and closing deals with enterprises and government agencies.  •    Adapt to emerging technologies and changing market landscapes to propose innovative IT solutions. [What we are looking for] •    Relevant qualification in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering or a related field. •    At least 10 years of professional experience in the IT industry, with a strong technical foundation in artificial intelligence and other emerging technologies.  •    Proven ability to build and nurture high-performing teams. •    Demonstrated success in capability development, business development, business growth, and technology transformation. •    Extensive experience in developing and deploying IT solutions involving artificial intelligence and other emerging technologies, including leading the creation and launch of artificial intelligence powered services. •    Experience in collaborating with government agencies, research institutes, and industry partners. •    Excellent communication, stakeholder engagement, and influencing skills, including the ability to engage senior management, external partners, and internal teams."
    },
