      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] School of Infocomm – Associate Lecturer (Cybersecurity & Digital Forensics) [What you will be working on] You will be involved in the following to support our full time and part-time course offerings in areas related to Penetration Testing/Red Teaming, Web Application and Cloud Security, SOC Operations, IT Audit & Compliance, Digital Forensics, and other foundational ICT modules. • Implement and administer module delivery, related activities (including student assessments and assignments) to meet learning outcomes. • Deliver module curriculum, learning activities and materials. • Stay current and responsive to changing developments in the profession and educational landscape. • Maintain links with industry to stay current and to promote collaborations. [What we are looking for] Applicants should have a relevant qualification preferably in the fields of IT/Computer Science, with a minimum of 1 year's industry experience. Industry certifications such as CISSP, CISA, CISM, CEH and OSCP will be a plus.  Applicants should be proficient in two or more of the following areas:  •    Penetration Testing/Red Teaming •    SOC operations, Firewall Configuration  •    Cloud Security, Web Application Security  •    IT Audit and Compliance, Personal Data Protection  •    Digital Forensics"
