risk management, or regulatory compliance. •    Passion for developing youths and adult learners through innovative and applied learning approaches. •    Strong communication, facilitation, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage PET students, adult learners, colleagues, and industry partners effectively. •    Ability to lead projects, build industry partnerships and work collaboratively across multidisciplinary teams. •    Experience in teaching, curriculum development, or training will be an advantage."
