    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Singapore/School-of-Management-and-Communication---Lecturer--Human-Resource-Management-with-Psychology---EG-_JR-10000004202": {
      "title": "School of Business - Lecturer (Human Resource Management with Psychology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] As part of the academic team in the Diploma in Human Resources with Psychology (DHRMP), you will play a key role in shaping the next generation of HR and career counselling professionals through applied learning and industry engagement. [What you will be working on] •    Facilitate learning for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education & Training (CET) learners through interactive seminar, workshop, coaching, and experiential learning activities.  •    Design, review and deliver industry-relevant curriculum in areas such as:           Full HR functions         -     HR Analytics & HR Technology (AI)         -     Strategic and Operational HR Functions          -     Industrial & Organisational Psychology          -     Positive Psychology          -     Psychometric Assessment          -     Socio-emotional Counselling  •    Lead and supervise student-industry collaboration projects, applying real-world HR practices to authentic workplace challenges.  •    Partner with industry stakeholders to develop consultancy, applied research, and capability development projects.  •    Build and maintain strong industry networks to create meaningful opportunities for students, including mentorships, industry projects, internships, and award sponsorships.  •    Mentor and guide students in their academic, professional, and personal development journey.  This role is well-suited for experienced HR, career counselling, psychology, or organisational development professionals who are keen to leverage their industry expertise to develop future HR leaders, and make a meaningful impact through education. [What we are looking for] •    Relevant qualifications in Human Resource Management, Psychology, Career Counselling, Organisational Development, or related disciplines.  •    Professional accreditation and/or membership with recognised bodies would be advantageous, not limiting to:          -     NCDA credentials          -     IHRP certification  •    At least 5 years of relevant industry experience in HR, career counselling, psychology, organisational development, or related fields.  •    Strong industry networks and the ability to engage organisations on applied projects, collaborations, and talent development initiatives.  •    Passionate about developing people and nurturing future-ready professionals.  •    Strong communication, stakeholder management, and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple initiatives effectively.  You will thrive in this role if you are looking for an opportunity to transition from industry into academia while continuing to stay connected to industry practices, contribute to workforce capability development, and influence the future of the profession."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Sports-and-Health-Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Integrated-Community-Care-_JR-10000049638": {
      "title": "School of Sports and Health-Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Integrated Community Care)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Sports and Health – Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Diploma in Integrated Community Care) The School of Sports and Health, whose vision is to be a leading educator in the domains of sports, health, and community care, invites qualified and passionate candidates to apply for the position of Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in the Diploma in Integrated Community Care (DICC). [What you will be working on] The Diploma in Integrated Community Care aims to prepare students for emerging roles in Singapore’s evolving health and social care landscape. The programme equips learners with competencies to support integrated care models that span healthcare, social services, and community-based support systems. The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer will: •    Deliver academic and instructional duties for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes. •    Design, review, and update curriculum to ensure relevance to the sector and uphold academic governance. •    Facilitate student learning through experiential, practice-based approaches and mentor students in their holistic development. •    Supervise students in final-year projects, internships, overseas study trips, and co-curricular activities. •    Develop and maintain partnerships with healthcare providers, community organisations, and social service agencies to support applied learning and research. •    Contribute to applied research and development projects that promote innovation in integrated community care delivery. •    Take part in school-wide administrative duties, event organisation, outreach activities, and other committee roles. [What we are looking for] •    Relevant qualification in nursing, allied health, social work, public health, health administration, or a related discipline.  •    At least 3–5 years of relevant experience in the community care or healthcare sector (e.g., aged care, primary care, integrated care settings, ILTC providers, VWOs, or public health institutions). •    Working knowledge and/or experience in areas such as: o    Integrated care models and frameworks o    Community health and social care coordination o    Gerontology and active ageing o    Health promotion and chronic disease management o    Multi-disciplinary care planning •    Familiarity with local health and social care systems and government initiatives (e.g., Healthier SG, Community Networks for Seniors) is preferred. •    Passionate about education, student development, and building manpower for the integrated care sector. •    Self-motivated, team-oriented, and committed to delivering high-quality teaching and project outcomes. •    Strong communication, planning, and organisation skills, with attention to detail."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Sports-and-Health-Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Outdoor-Education-_JR-10000053468": {
      "title": "School of Sports and Health-Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Outdoor Education)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The School of Sports and Health invites passionate and driven individuals to join its dynamic team in advancing sports, health and outdoor education. The Diploma in Outdoor Education (DOE) team aspires to be a recognised thought leader and trusted partner in research, training and development within the outdoor education, recreation and inclusive practice sectors. [What you will be working on] Job Responsibilities The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer for the Diploma in Outdoor Education will contribute to teaching, curriculum development, student mentoring, programme delivery and industry engagement in the following areas: Deliver quality Pre-Employment Training (PET) modules and Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes in outdoor education and related areas, including: • Climbing and Abseiling  • Kayaking  • Challenge Course Management • Land-based outdoor skills such as campcraft and navigation • Supervision and management  • Instruction and Facilitation  • Adventure and experiential education • Youth Outreach and Development  • Environmental studies and Nature interpretation  • Expedition Management • Demonstrate a strong commitment to holistic student development, including mentoring, guidance, and support for students’ academic, personal, and professional growth. • Serve as a positive role model for students, exemplifying professionalism, integrity, care, and responsible conduct in all learning and engagement contexts. Develop, review and enhance curriculum to ensure alignment with current industry practices, applied research, safety standards and emerging trends in outdoor education. • Design and facilitate authentic, experiential and student-centred learning experiences that develop students’ technical competence, confidence, leadership, resilience and reflective practice. • Uphold robust safety, risk management and operational standards during practical lessons, field-based learning, expeditions and outdoor programmes. • Build and sustain partnerships with industry, community and professional bodies to support curriculum relevance, student development, applied projects and continuing education opportunities. [What we are looking for] • Relevant qualifications in outdoor education, sports, recreation, education, health, or related discipline, with at least 5 years of relevant industry experience. • Good written and oral communication skills. • Strong time management, organisational and administrative skills, with the ability to manage multiple responsibilities and meet deadlines. • Agility to learn and adapt to changes. • Demonstrates a strong passion for outdoor education, with responsibility, reliability,  independence, initiative in problem-solving, resourcefulness and the ability to work effectively in a team. • Strong communication and interpersonal skills to establish and maintain quality working relationships with students, colleagues, and stakeholders. • Proficient in the following methods of instruction and facilitation skills: o            Group management skills o            Group facilitation and review skills o            Presentation and lecturing skills o            Programme/game design and lesson planning skills • Preferably holds relevant certifications in outdoor and adventure skills such as: o            Kayak Level 3 Coaching and/or o            Climbing Instructor Category 2 and/or  o            Abseiling Level 3. o            First Aid and CPR AED certification • Experience in designing and conducting programmes for participants with disabilities, older adults or children will be an advantage."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Technology-for-Arts--Media---Design---AD--Capability---Industry-_JR-10000054113": {
      "title": "School of Technology for Arts, Media & Design - AD (Capability & Industry)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The Assistant Director (Capability & Industry) is a strategic and hands-on leader responsible for driving consultancy, applied research, intellectual property development, and external industry engagement for the School of Technology for Arts, Media and Design. This role leads the development and execution of strategies that strengthen the School’s staff capability, grow consultancy and applied research activity, and expand the School’s industry relevance beyond the traditional creative sector. We are looking for individuals with the ability to lead cross-functional teams, provide leadership on complex and novel issues and shape policies, practices, and partnerships that advance the School’s strategic objectives. This role is critical in positioning the School of Technology for the Arts, Media and Design as a strategic partner to industry, both within the creative sector and across the wider economy. By shaping functional priorities, building staff capability, driving applied consultancy, research, and intellectual property development, and opening new industry pathways, the Assistant Director enables the School to strengthen industry relevance, create reusable intellectual assets, and deliver meaningful, sustainable impact beyond traditional academic boundaries. [What you will be working on] Spearhead consultancy, applied research, and industry engagement initiatives to strengthen the School’s industry-facing capabilities and impact. Develop and implement functional strategies, policies, and frameworks to drive sustainable growth and measurable impact. Address novel and complex challenges by integrating creative, arts, design, and media perspectives and disciplines with industry needs. Drive the identification, structuring, and delivery of consultancy and applied research projects, including opportunities to generate intellectual property particularly with non-creative industry and government partners. Identify and pursue collaborative projects with industry partners, developing tailored solutions that draw on STA’s strengths in digital media solutions, immersive experiences, design-led innovation, and Designing Your Life facilitation. Enhance consultancy models, processes, and service quality by applying best practices to improve intellectual property and revenue generation, and project outcomes. Coach and mentor staff, building School-wide capability in consultancy delivery, industry-facing research, and professional practice. Lead upskilling initiatives and foster cross-disciplinary collaboration to address skill gaps. Build and maintain strategic partnerships with corporates, agencies, research institutions, and solution providers. Influence School and institutional leaders to adopt new approaches and priorities, and negotiate with external partners to achieve mutually beneficial outcomes. Work across functions and schools to align resources, manage dependencies, and optimise results, exercising autonomy and sound judgement. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in arts, media, design, creative technologies, business, engineering or a related discipline. Significant professional experience in business development, industry partnerships, consultancy, applied research, innovation or related industry-facing roles. Demonstrated success in capability development, consultancy growth, applied research, intellectual property development, industry engagement and stakeholder partnership development. Proven experience in translating creative or design-led strengths into industry-relevant solutions for non-Arts, Design and Media sector organizations. Experience developing or supporting tailored industry solutions in areas such as arts and digital media, immersive experiences, and related domains. Strong track record in influencing stakeholders, negotiating with external partners, and driving change across complex stakeholder environments. Ability to operate independently and confidently in complex, ambiguous and evolving environments, with sound judgement and accountability for outcomes."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/COI-SCM---Manager-Senior-Manager_JR-10000038982": {
      "title": "Centre of Innovation for Supply Chain Management – Manager/Senior Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Centre of Innovation for Supply Chain Management – Manager/Senior Manager [What you will be working on] • Able to quickly understand company's logistics and supply chain capabilities to meet business needs to propose relevant consultancy and technology solutions • Execute end-to-end supply chain and logistics process review for process, digitalisation, AI, visibility, IoT and Warehouse Automation Opportunities • Implement innovative and impactful digitalisation, LEAN process and warehouse automation projects to industry  • Support outreach events with setup and assisting in demonstrations  [What we are looking for] Business development:  • A driven self-starter that actively keeps abreast with business needs and can quickly put together proof-of-concepts to meet business needs  • Sell to both business leaders and operations staff the benefits of process and technology innovation • Strong collaborator with internal and external stakeholders to execute impactful supply chain projects Familiarity in implementing:  • Process improvement using LEAN, swimlane and other process discovery tools • practical Warehouse Automation possibilities and technology trends • Office 365 tools (including Power Automate, PowerBl, SharePoint, Power Apps, etc) and Google Workspace/ Cloud tools like Google Appsheet  • Motivated to explore, learn and apply new technologies in warehouse automation, AI and physical AI"
    }
